# --- The redaction list itself (2026-09-27) ---------------------------------
# scripts/build_collections.py must redact a withheld identifier at document-
# build time, and it must NOT name it: this repository is published, so a name
# written as a literal in a tracked script is published, and the redaction
# defeats itself. The identifier is held here instead, in a file that is never
# tracked. `git rm --cached .redaction.local.json` if it is ever added by
# mistake; there is no substitute for it in the tree.
#
# Shape:
#   { "names": ["<identifier to withhold>", ...],
#     "marker": "<the visible marker substituted in its place>" }
#
# If this file is absent the build still succeeds - a public clone has no
# capture files either and must not be broken by this - but NOTHING is redacted
# and build_collections.py prints a loud warning naming this path. It is not
# obfuscated, encoded or split anywhere in the tree; there is no copy to find.
.redaction.local.json

# --- Publication redaction (P1, 2026-09-27) ---------------------------------
# Two categories of material are kept out of the PUBLISHED repository. Both are
# withheld, not edited: the bytes are evidence, so the working tree keeps them
# and only the git index drops them. The controller applies
# `git rm --cached <path>` for each; see the per-file notes below before
# removing anything from disk as well.
#
# 1. Three raw WebVTT caption captures of his own conversion-story video. They
#    contain his BIRTH NAME. Verbatim source evidence, so they are untracked
#    rather than redacted. The reader-facing text built from them is served
#    under /_transcripts/.
#
#    PER-FILE, because they are NOT interchangeable and all three are
#    load-bearing. Corrected 2026-09-27: the first rule below named
#    cap-7KBCENktOUU, which is not a file that exists, so the capture that
#    actually holds the birth name was not ignored and would have been
#    published by `git add -A`. The real name is cap-7KBCENktOOU.
#      cap-7KBCENktOOU  - REQUIRED ON DISK. Named by the coverage row for video
#                         7KBCENktOOU (15,048 lines).
#      cap-D2t0idkAqjA  - REQUIRED ON DISK. Named by that row's `alternates`,
#                         re-parented onto 7KBCENktOOU; the page published at
#                         /transcripts/D2t0idkAqjA-duplicate-upload/ is built
#                         from it.
#      cap-G47Stp3pLss  - REQUIRED ON DISK. The only capture named by the
#                         coverage row for video G47Stp3pLss.
#    scripts/test_transcripts.py re-derives all 68 published transcripts from
#    the capture files the coverage data names, so `git rm --cached` is correct
#    for all three and DELETING any of them from disk is not: it breaks the
#    suite and orphans a served page.
#    Do NOT blanket-ignore .firecrawl/ - 26 further captures and 39 whisper
#    JSONs in that directory are named by the coverage file and are load-bearing.
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-7KBCENktOOU.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-D2t0idkAqjA.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-G47Stp3pLss.en-orig.vtt
#
# 2. One held PDF whose provenance could not be verified against any public
#    source URL, so the archive declines to publish it. Already removed from the
#    served tree and from its _data row; this rule only stops it being re-added.
_papers/pdfs/architects-of-civilisation-sallahuddin-ayubi.pdf

# --- Publication redaction (2026-09-29, caption lane) ------------------------
# Ten of the eleven caption captures taken for the thirteen verified-missing
# videos. These are UNLABELLED automatic speech recognition of live audience
# questions, so they carry whatever a member of the public said when handed the
# microphone - and some of them said their own names.
#
# Withheld, not edited, for the same reason as category 1: the bytes are
# evidence that the recording says what it says, so the working tree keeps them
# and only the git index drops them.
#
# WHAT IS AND IS NOT REDACTED IN THE SERVED TEXT, stated accurately. An earlier
# version of this comment said the reader-facing text "passes through the
# redaction list", which overstated it. The redaction list holds exactly one
# identifier - the author's withheld birth name - and it does not touch these
# captures. The transcripts derived from the ten files below are published AS
# SPOKEN, on the owner's explicit decision after being told what they contain,
# under the existing machine-transcript warning. That decision covers
# third-party names, including a participant who gives his own name on air, and
# it is a disclosure choice rather than an oversight. Withholding the raw bytes
# from git is a separate decision, taken because unlabelled ASR of a live
# audience is not what a public repository should hand out as source material.
#
# The sharpest three, and why each is here rather than merely untidy:
#   7EqMJJuUKr8  a participant states his legal name on air, on the record,
#                after giving a religious name
#   0biKKRHO_Tk  a full personal name, plus employer sector and country
#   kRCzZW3rg4U  he criticises a named community member and thanks a named
#                moderator. These are people he names, not his own family, and
#                publishing the criticism verbatim attaches it to them.
#
# cap-MCR3xh8wccQ is deliberately NOT in this section: it is the one capture of
# the eleven that screened clean, and it is tracked like the other 26.
#
# Do NOT blanket-ignore .firecrawl/ - see the warning above; captures named by
# _data/transcript_coverage.json are load-bearing for scripts/test_transcripts.py,
# which re-derives every published transcript from the file its coverage row
# names. All eleven below are REQUIRED ON DISK. `git rm --cached` is correct;
# deleting any of them from disk is not.
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-QoU02Om_wiQ.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-n3vhs1mcmVM.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-OHNMeqGMdPc.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-lE690yapgTA.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-idz29r5LHig.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-7EqMJJuUKr8.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-0biKKRHO_Tk.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-3vqVYfs5mCk.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-kRCzZW3rg4U.en-orig.vtt
.firecrawl/transcripts/cap-M3nB154Mkuk.en-orig.vtt

# llms-full.txt is a DERIVED artifact of scripts/build_llms_full.py, and the
# file stamps the date it was generated. Committing it would dirty the
# repository every single day on a 6.8 MB file that changes only in that date
# line. CI runs the generator as a build step and 
pm run build runs it from
# prebuild, so nothing needs it tracked.
#
# llms.txt IS tracked, deliberately: it is hand-written, reviewed, and part of
# what a reader is being told. Only the generated concatenation is not.
llms-full.txt
